course: dictionary
lesson: 15806
title: Unborn and the future
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «unborn» is made of two parts. Un- means not, and born means having come into the world. So unborn means not yet born.
explain: «The unborn baby was still growing inside her mum, and it would not arrive until spring.» The clue «until spring» tells you the baby has not arrived yet, so unborn means not yet born.
explain: Unborn can also look forward in time. «We must keep the forests safe for generations yet unborn.» Those people do not exist yet, but they will be born one day. Try the meaning in the sentence: «generations not yet born» still makes sense.
fact: The prefix un- often means not, as in unhappy, unkind and unborn.
fact: «Unborn» means not yet born.
fact: An unborn baby grows inside its mother for about nine months.
fact: «Generations yet unborn» means people of the future, who have not been born yet.
fact: Unborn is an adjective: it describes a noun, as in «an unborn baby» or «the unborn child».
exercise: «The unborn baby was still growing inside her mum.» What does unborn mean here? | Lost forever | *Not yet born | Very tiny and cold | Already grown up
exercise: «We must look after the land for generations yet unborn.» Who are generations yet unborn? | Animals in the park | People who have died | Our grandparents | *People who will be born in the future
exercise: Which part of the word unborn means not? | the | *un- | unborn | born
test: Ellie says the unborn baby is already a toddler. Is she right? | Yes, because babies are always unborn | *No, a toddler has already been born | Yes, toddlers are always unborn | Maybe, it depends on the weather
test: Which word is the opposite of unborn? | *born | future | unborn | baby
exam: «Mum said the unborn twins would arrive in May.» What does unborn mean here? | Lost in the hospital | Born last year | Already born and asleep | *Not yet born
